{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgRZEMYYGSYU6468mnqrs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"ANSWER: The Apollo 13 Review Board was chaired by Edgar Cortright, who was director of NASA Langley Research Center at the time. The board traced the explosion to an electrically started fire in oxygen tank No. 2, caused by its thermostatic switches. The switches were built to a 1962 specification for 28-volt DC, and the heater specification was later revised to 65 volts without changing the switches. The board called the failure a serious oversight that all parties shared, and recommended redesigning the tank and removing electrical equipment from inside it.\n\nFILES:\n- areas/apollo-13-review-board.md\n- sources/apollo-13-review-board-report.md\n- people/edgar-cortright.md\n- topics/oxygen-tank-2.md"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1339,"cache_read_input_tokens":26360,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1339,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d88c4e6a-14bf-4d5c-a78d-f368a5fc145a","uuid":"9f3714a9-1027-492a-8ae7-8fb5929c8b78","timestamp":"2026-10-26T21:26:50.303Z","request_id":"req_011CgRZEMAU9siyECzeQRKxB"}
